      `drive-sim` IS NOT A DOSE COLUMN. Its U and tau_rec are PINNED at
      §68's operating point for every arm, by design, so that it is §68's
      statistic verbatim wherever it appears. It therefore varies across
      this ladder only through the dose's effect on SPIKE COUNTS, and it
      is comparable with the measured drive AT tau300 AND NOWHERE ELSE.

      -> A SUFFICIENT DOSE DOES PUT IT IN THE DRIVE: stp tau3000 reads 0.8377 on
         a testable oracle, so "the measured drive never carries the
         conjunction" is REFUTED. A selected maximum is allowed to do
         this and nothing more — the cell is chosen on the data, and
         what it licenses is the falsification, not the figure.

