      dose; they are not a verdict.

    THE CONSEQUENCE — does the SIMULATION flatter the mechanism?
      §68's drive minus the kernel's, paired, same trials and units
      +0.1409 +- 0.0141  (10.0 SE)   THE SIMULATION READS HIGHER

    -> AT §68's OWN OPERATING POINT ITS SEPARATION DOES NOT TRANSFER AT
       FULL SIZE. The level offset is §68's disclosed optimism and is
       not the finding; what matters is that a readout of the SIMULATED
       drive beats a readout of the REAL one on the same trials, so
       §68's figure at tau300 was inflated by the simulation and not
       only by its flag. This comparison is valid HERE and nowhere else
       on the ladder, because `drive-sim`'s parameters are pinned to
       this dose.
    -> AT §68's OWN OPERATING POINT THE CONJUNCTION IS NOT IN THE
       MEASURED DRIVE AS A READOUT CAN USE IT, and the scope of that
       sentence is the whole of it. A held-out readout of the drive the
       kernel actually delivers does not reach the bar at tau300, so
       §68's pair-d' priced an ORACLE OVER PAIRS — handed the pairing,
       scoring a scalar — and never a single-trial readout. At THIS
       dose nothing downstream can be at fault, because the membrane
       and the spikes cannot lose a signal that is not in what reaches
       them. WHETHER A LARGER DOSE CHANGES THIS IS A SEPARATE QUESTION
       AND THE DOSE LADDER ABOVE ANSWERS IT — read it before carrying
       this sentence anywhere, because it does NOT generalise.

